WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.530
kikoeru ka kikoeru darou

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.530
<i>Can you hear it? I'm sure you can...</i>

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.360
harukana todoroki

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.360
<i>...that faraway roar!</i>

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.530
yami no naka kokoro yusaburu

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.530
<i>Your soul trembles in the darkness</i>

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.700
mezame hajimaru

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.700
<i>as it begins to awaken</i>

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.750
daichi wari sosoritatsu sugata

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.750
<i>A towering figure shatters the earth</i>

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
seigi no akashi ka

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>Is it the symbol of justice?</i>

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.010
densetsu no kyojin no chikara

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>The legendary giant's power</i>

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.970
ginga kirisaku

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.970
<i>will tear through the galaxy!</i>

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.220
otakebi ga denkou sekka no

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.220
<i>Our war cry will summon</i>

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.060
ichigeki wo yobu

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.060
<i>a flash of lightning!</i>

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.100
furueru na hitomi korase yo

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>Have no fear, focus your eyes on...</i>

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.480
fukkatsu no toki

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.480
<i>the moment of resurrection!</i>

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.240
hito yo inochi yo hajimari wo miru

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.240
<i>Mankind and all life witness it begin</i>

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:03.160
<i>Space Runaway ldeon, Ideon</i>

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.170
<i>Space Runaway Ideon, Ideon</i>

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.750
On her way back to the Buff Clan homeworld,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:34.100
Harulu Ajiba was caught by Cosmo and the Solo Ship.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:47.540
However, the Ideon's abnormal powerup resulted
 in its parts splitting up, causing a tough fight.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.460
The two ships were locked in a short-range battle.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.220
Although it looked like Harulu had lost the fight,

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:01.340
she was able to escape due to new reinforcements.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:08.060
They got away!

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:14.070
<b>The Shocking Decoy Planet</b>

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.040
This is colony planet number 1-7, Caral!

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:27.950
Aliens... An unknown group of aliens...

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.040
has come to attack us.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.920
Please help us.

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:33.310
This is colony planet number 1-7, Caral!

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:34.300
Caral!

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.550
A half of our planet has already
 been destroyed! Please send help!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.880
Please send help!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.370
This is colony planet number 1-7...

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.330
This is Caral! Caral!

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.400
Please help us!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.400
Caral! Caral!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.680
When was this transmission sent?

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.350
About 30 minutes ago.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.560
We suddenly picked it up on our
 interstellar transmission channel.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.480
I see.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.240
Listen, everyone.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.280
Should we go to Caral?

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.110
Aliens, huh?

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.660
I'm against it.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.410
I don't want a repeat of Ajian.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.990
But it could be the Buff Clan, you know!

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.290
We have to go help them!

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.450
Do you want to die that badly, Deck?

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.670
Well, no, but...

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:20.130
When Planet Solo was attacked, you
wanted to be saved, didn't you, Sheryl?

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:23.890
It's not about us living or dying.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:24.970
We need to help.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.180
But what's the Ideon's power like right now?

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.020
Can we control it?

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.830
We're looking into that.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.750
How many days will it take to reach Caral?

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.070
Less than three days.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.190
We'll think it over during that time.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.250
Stay down, Lou, you'll get something later.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.710
Aww, jeez...

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.470
Why you!

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.650
Don't mess around!

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:16.660
Ow!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.020
Don't whine.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.530
I'm servicing you for free, you know.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.490
I wouldn't bother getting a haircut otherwise!

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.030
How's your research progressing, Sheryl?

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.810
I can't seem to find any correlation...

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.480
between the Ideon Gauge's changes
and the pilot's brainwaves.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.130
That's not surprising.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.130
I mean, it was moving on its own at first.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.820
But I have confirmed that the power
 goes up when the pilot feels fear.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.300
So does the Ideon become stronger
 if we all just start panicking?

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.390
I wish it was that simple...

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:58.020
From an engineer's standpoint, do you
 understand the Ide's control mechanism?

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:02.840
There's some sort of a magnetic field
surrounding the main engine that we can't break.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.700
If its power really is infinite, we could
 launch an offensive of our own!

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.080
And wipe out the Buff Clan for good?

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.660
It might be possible!

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.420
And Deck and Lou will hail you as a hero!

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.120
Is there something wrong with that?

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.370
So this is Caral?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.970
Are there really people living here?

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.820
Yes... I'm certain this is Caral.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:52.540
It's almost like Earth during the Precambrian period...

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.040
The other hemisphere has
 been completely destroyed.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.660
We can't detect any aliens.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.290
It must have been the Buff Clan.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.290
This looks the same as Ajian.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:04.090
So they used the sub-light missiles?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.140
Even a single Zan-class ship with
 sub-light missiles could have done this.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.730
It was the Buff Clan after all!

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.550
Damn them!

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.870
Cosmo! They must be somewhere near here, right?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.140
All right, Deck.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:16.850
Let's go!

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:17.980
I'm ready!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.190
All Ideon units, launch for reconnaissance!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.520
Everyone on the Solo Ship,  take battle preparations.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:32.870
There!

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.900
Kasha, Moera, let's spread out and scout the area!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:07.940
Roger!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:08.990
Roger!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.120
Altitude 100! Keep your eyes open!

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.240
We may not find any survivors even with our sensors.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.040
Yeah.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:19.750
H-Hey!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.140
That's a crater left by a single sub-light missile!

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:34.340
What if there were no survivors?

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.380
This looks like a scene from hell.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.750
I wouldn't be surprised if we  bumped into the devil itself!

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.420
Watch the altitude.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:47.730
Okay, okay.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.210
This place looks a bit better than the previous areas.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.330
Deck, don't take your eyes off the sensor.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.130
Yeah, I know!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:11.670
Cosmo!

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:12.800
I've caught something on the sensor!

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.880
Okay, show it on the video monitor!

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:15.620
Roger!

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.350
Over there?

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:21.830
I can't tell for sure, but they seem like survivors.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.940
Land in front and we'll check it out.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:51.380
Hey, is there anyone over there?

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:00.310
Cosmo!

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.980
How many people are there?

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:13.610
Who told you to fire?!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:15.320
Well...

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.200
They might be on our side!

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.450
Don't do anything until we're sure!

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:20.070
Understand?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:21.580
Got it!

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.890
Stop shooting! I'm an Earthling!

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:33.880
Do you hear me?

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.090
Shut up!

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.800
You attacked us too!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.220
Stop firing!

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.720
We've come here to help!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.140
We're not the Buff Clan!

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:47.140
See, you've shown your true colors!

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.940
No one said anything about the Buff Clan!

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:50.940
That's right, get outta here!

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:55.940
Where'd he go?

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:56.990
Find him!

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.810
Looks like I'll have to resort to force...

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.200
Where? Where are you?

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:03.740
Answer me!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.580
Sis, what'll we do?

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:08.790
Don't worry.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:11.460
A woman and children?

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.180
Aren't they Earthlings?

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.210
Over there!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.300
Wait, don't fire!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:20.340
Get out!

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.810
What's so suspicious about me?

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.850
Cosmo!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.980
Something's coming!

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.190
Deck, get back!

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:36.650
Huh? It's a kid...

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.200
Something's approaching us at high speed!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.120
Isn't it Kasha and the others?

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.080
No, they won't answer our identifier signal!

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.580
Hey, can you hear me?

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:49.910
Cease your fire for now!

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:50.870
The aliens are coming!

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.960
You'll be in danger there! Hide somewhere!

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:54.840
There he is!

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:55.710
Don't shoot!

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:56.550
Huh?

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.000
He's somehow different...

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.470
Deck, where are the enemies?

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.010
They should be in sight already.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.510
Raise the engine output!

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.430
It's at 50% now.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.440
Over there...

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.140
Deck, contact Kasha and the others!

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:13.860
Roger!

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.510
You fell for it!

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.930
I knew you'd show up if I attacked this planet...

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.670
Deck, we need to escape fast! Prepare for lift off!

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.340
Roger!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.600
Show me what you can do!

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:53.140
Deck, fire the bottom missiles!

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.100
I'm doing it!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.710
Everyone, we've got to get underground quickly.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:19.630
Come on, hurry up!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.020
It's fast!

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.260
If they're scientifically on the
 same level as us like Gije said,

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:40.890
I should have no problem defeating them!

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:46.490
Deck, fire the beam!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:47.160
Roger!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:48.370
Locked on...

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.080
Fire!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:57.920
A barrier?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.040
Deck, concentrate the beam on one point!

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.420
The missiles, too!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.840
You're in trouble if you think this is your
 average military Heavy Mobile Mecha!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.520
Cosmo!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:25.810
Now you can't turn into the Giant,
 even if your friends show up!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:26.450
Damn it!

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:28.060
He caught the Ideo-Delta!

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:32.790
Should I try it?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.010
Is it trying to free itself from my Ganga Lubu?

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:44.570
We're going to crash!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:46.630
Go!

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:04.720
He's got some skills.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:07.650
Deck!

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:08.450
Are you alright?

00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:09.530
Yeah, I'm alright!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:10.720
Where's the enemy?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:11.570
Cosmo!

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.450
Is it alright?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:14.700
Kasha?

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:16.160
Oh, I see them.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.040
The Ideo-Nova and the Ideo-Buster.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:18.580
Okay!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:19.370
Let's dock!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.040
Deck, don't let the enemy close to us!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:21.630
Roger!

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:24.960
Here they are!

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:26.800
Gije! Do you hear me?

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:27.550
Yes sir!

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.560
The enemy is about to dock!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:30.640
Roger!

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.330
That's Cosmo!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.970
It looks the like the enemy's chasing him!

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:38.640
Kasha, Kasha!

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:39.310
Cosmo?!

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.270
Let's dock!

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.100
Get into position!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:42.650
Wait!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.020
Something's coming from below!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.110
To the left!

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:49.110
It's too late!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:55.600
I haven't seen that Heavy Mobile Mecha before!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:56.870
What incredible fire power!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:58.410
It's coming, rise up!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.460
Now, let's dock!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:08.300
Roger!

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.610
I won't let you!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:33.440
The barrier is breaking!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:34.860
I can't get into docking formation!

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.080
I won't let you form the Giant!

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.100
This is the power of the barrier-breaking
 Donovan particles!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.500
Gije, what are you doing?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.080
Help me destroy their barrier!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.500
This is Gije, moving up!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:53.010
Impossible...

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.070
How's that?!

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.940
Moera, let's dock at high speed!

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:10.630
Got that?

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:11.290
Roger!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.450
Barrier destroyer, Donovan!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:21.370
Get outta the way!

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.830
He cut the barrier!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:39.430
It's quick!

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:42.080
How clever! A barrier destroyer?

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:48.810
Too slow!

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.990
The missile launcher!

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.300
Damn Giant, don't take me so lightly!

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:15.050
Sir Daram!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:29.940
Gije!

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:31.440
I've put a nuclear bomb on them.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:32.570
Get us out of here, now!

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.440
A nuclear bomb?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:37.910
Running away?!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:00.800
Sir Daram...

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.260
Despite its small size, that's just
 as powerful as a nuclear explosive.

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.470
The Giant is done for.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.350
I'm only testing it.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:07.480
Testing?

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:08.310
That's right!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.770
If the Giant can't take a direct
 hit from a nuclear weapon,

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:14.400
then it's of no worth to us.

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:37.800
Cosmo, what on earth was that?

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.300
That explosion...

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.640
It wasn't just an ordinary bomb!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.600
Cosmo, what was that just now?

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:47.730
Was there some kind of explosion to our left side?

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:49.560
The shock was horrible.

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.400
We'll investigate it later.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.730
Shouldn't we scout out the evacuees first?

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:55.730
You're right.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.490
Deck, I'm handing it over to you.

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.110
I'll take it from here.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:00.360
Just take it easy, Cosmo.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.990
Ah, thanks.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.220
I see...

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.550
That Giant can even withstand a nuclear blast?

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:24.470
Yes...

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:28.020
I'm glad to see it's just as 
powerful as we expected, but...

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.350
In that case, how shall we seize it?

00:19:30.510 --> 00:19:33.290
The aliens are mentally similar to us.

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.190
We can take advantage of that!

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.160
However, there's one thing I'm anxious about, Gije.

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.570
The legend says that the
 Ide shines for the righteous.

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:45.210
Can we say for certain that we
 are righteous in our battle?

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:50.000
We need the Ide's power in order to
overthrow Zuou's dictatorship!

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.750
That is true.

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:53.070
Doba believes that, too.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.800
We've been given orders to capture the
Giant from the Orme Foundation.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.460
These ships and supplies are for that purpose.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.960
Don't stop believing in what we're fighting for.

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:12.810
You guys were controlling this giant thing?

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:14.890
No way!

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.810
I'm not lying, it's true!

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.360
Once you get a hang of it, it's relatively simple.

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:21.900
Can I try using it then?

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:24.950
Huh? No, you can't do that...

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:28.740
Why? If you can do it, why couldn't we?

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.750
No, I don't mean that, but...

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.120
Stingy!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.880
I bet you can't fly it!

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:36.960
That's not true!

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.840
I don't believe you!

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:40.090
Kitty Kitten.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.720
Kitten...

00:20:46.150 --> 00:20:47.580
I'm sorry about what happened before.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:53.860
But the Buff Clan aliens may not
have come if it wasn't for you.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.810
That can't be true.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.560
I hope so.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.780
But even my father died, as a soldier.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:02.700
Just like those kid's parents...

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:05.490
I want you to leave.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:06.280
Right away.

00:21:06.810 --> 00:21:10.490
Yeah, we'll leave once we get
 some weapons and ammunition.

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:11.640
That's impossible!

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:13.540
Out of the question!

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:14.460
But why?

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:17.670
We can hardly fight because
we have so few weapons!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:22.210
We need the cooperation of Caral's defense
force if we're going to beat the Buff Clan!

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:26.300
We've lost more than half our forces! 
There's nothing left to spare!

00:21:26.540 --> 00:21:28.800
Make do with what you have!

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:29.450
Excuse me.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:31.560
But...!

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:34.970
Isn't this the way it was on Ajian?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.020
Yes...

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.500
It can't be helped.

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:42.570
Yeah, but...

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.190
We're struggling desperately too!

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:52.240
But all the people here who lost family
 members think of you as an enemy.

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:53.790
Can you blame them?

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.830
Everyone on the Solo Ship lost their relatives too!

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:00.330
You're not the only ones suffering!

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.130
Cosmo...?

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:10.550
Is there anyone who actually likes killing?

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:30.960
You're right...

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:38.830
To meet new people only to be cast aside.

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:45.170
Is this the fate given to the Solo Ship?

00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:53.050
<i>The Solo Ship tries to negotiate
 with the military of Caral.</i>

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:58.860
<i>Using that oppoturnity, the new enemy Daram
 sends guerrillas to infiltrate the Ideon.</i>

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:05.190
<i>The Solo Ship is cornered 
when enemies take over the Ideon.</i>

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:08.900
<i>Cosmo and the others decide 
to break into the Ideon!</i>

